[00:47.99] Like snowfall, you cry a silent storm
[00:58.42] Your tears paint rivers on this oaken wall
[01:10.89] Amber nectar, misery ichor
[01:16.73] Cascading in streams of hallowed form
[01:27.38] For each stain, a forsaken shadow
[01:38.85] You are the lugubrious spirit
[01:45.33] Etched in the oak of wonder
[01:49.97] You are the sullen voice and silent storm
[02:15.77] Each night I lay
[02:17.26] Awakened by her shivering silent voice
[02:20.36] From the shapes in the corridor walls.
[02:24.66] It pierces the solitude like that of a distant scream
[02:28.75] In the pitch-black forest of my delusion
[02:44.76] With each passing day, a deeper grave
[02:54.22] Why did you leave me to die?
[02:58.19] Why did you abandon me?
[03:02.73] Why did you walk away and leave me bitterly yearning?"
[03:14.15] Her haunting, contorted despair was etched into the wood's grain
[03:28.74] Though fire rages within me, no fire burns fiercer than her desire
[03:39.78] The shape whispers my name
[06:11.83] I damn this oak
[06:16.62] I damn her sorrow
[06:21.74] I damn these oaken corridors
[06:25.50] That bear the ghosts of those I've thrown away
[06:31.58] Though tempted I am to caress her texture divine
[06:34.97] And taste her pain sweet, sweet like brandy wine
[06:39.82] I must burn these halls, these corridors
[06:44.53] And silence her shrill, tormenting voice
[06:49.42] Forever
[07:18.11] Like snowfall, you cried a silent storm
[07:28.49] No tears stain this dust in my hands
[07:40.11] But from this ashen gray, her voice still
[07:48.63] Whispers my name
[08:10.37] You were the lugubrious spirit
[08:16.85] Who haunted the oak of wonder
[08:20.72] You were the geist that warned this frozen silent storm
[08:29.62] You were but a ghost in my arms
[08:40.28] 